/** Jesús Gordillo — "the pivot's first-time finish": a signature riso film (iconic plays, FUTSAL; Gordillo is a pivot).
 *
 * WHO: Jesús García del Pino Gordillo (born 8 Feb 2001, Toledo, Spain), futsal PIVOT of (Illes Balears) Palma Futsal 2020–25 (No. 39),
 *  MFK Tyumen from July 2025, Spain U-19 European champion 2019 and Spain senior international (2026 Futsal Euro winner). The card
 *  (lib/town/playerAppearance.json country "Spain"; playerBios "Spanish pivot from Toledo who won the U-19 Euro in 2019, two Champions
 *  Leagues with Palma Futsal and the 2026 Futsal Euro with Spain") is the same person — no namesake / country mismatch. (Note for the lead:
 *  Wikipedia lists THREE Champions League titles with Palma, 2022–23, 2023–24 and 2024–25; the bio says two. Not changed here.)
 * WHY THIS MOMENT: his entry (lib/town/iconicPlays.json) is a signature — the pivot's first-time finish ("Be ready at the back post to
 *  finish first time") — not one match. The biggest documented goal of his career we could reach in writing is the OPENER of the 2025 UEFA
 *  Futsal Champions League FINAL: Palma Futsal 9–4 Kairat Almaty, 4 May 2025, 20:00, Antarès, Le Mans (France); Gordillo 6'03" (1–0).
 *  UEFA's report calls it "a rifled Jesús Gordillo opener – his second in two games"; Palma's own report says the pivot opened the scoring
 *  "para júbilo de los casi trescientos aficionados que teñían de verde una de las esquinas del pabellón" (to the joy of the almost three
 *  hundred fans who dyed one corner of the arena green). Neither source says HOW the goal was built or where on the court he struck it, so
 *  the film follows the brief's honest FALLBACK: the match chapter shows ONLY confirmed things (the final, the teams and their shirt colours,
 *  Palma's possession in Kairat's half, the scoreboard flipping to 1–0 on his goal, the green corner of fans, the 9–4 final score, the third
 *  title in a row) and never stages his shot; the move itself is a separate, clearly labelled demonstration in training tops.
 *  (Match choice: no futsal film uses the 2025 final — Luan Muller's film uses the 2025 SEMI-final two days earlier, Guitta's the 2019 final;
 *  Catela's film uses Spain 7–1 New Zealand at the 2024 World Cup, where Gordillo also scored.)
 * CAMERA PLAN:
 *  1  LIVE (broadcast camera HIGH in the main stand, looking across the court, real time): Palma (lime green) keep the ball in Kairat's half
 *     (Kairat in red); on "Early on" the camera tilts UP to the hanging scoreboard — the clock runs to 06:03 and the board flips 1–0 on
 *     "fires Palma" (the goal itself is OFF camera) — then tilts DOWN: the ball already in Kairat's net, Gordillo (No. 39) wheeling away
 *     toward the far corner, the green corner of fans jumping. On "Palma win" the camera tilts up again: 40:00, 9–4; down onto Palma's
 *     players jumping together; three yellow cups for three titles in a row.
 *  2  HOW HE DOES IT (demonstration, empty arena, real time; a LOW camera behind the play, left of centre): the winger dribbles down the left;
 *     Gordillo, back to goal, PINS his defender (leans into him, arm out); as the defender turns to watch the ball he SLIPS off the blind
 *     side to the BACK POST and waits, ready, body open; the winger rolls the ball across and he hits it FIRST TIME, no control touch, into
 *     the side the keeper has left. Goal.
 *  3  YOUR TURN (slow-motion replay of the demonstration from a HIGH coach's camera): his slip path drawn on the floor, the back-post ring
 *     ("Be ready"), the pass line, the first-time strike, a crossed-out extra touch and a tick. Lesson from the entry's `lesson`.
 * Sources (written; curl, 5 s apart, a generic User-Agent, 4 requests + the shared cache in scratchpad/films/src-cache/):
 *  - Wikipedia, "Jesús Gordillo" (raw, Sep 2026; wiki-jesus-gordillo.txt): full name, born 8 Feb 2001 in Toledo, Pivot, Palma Futsal
 *    2020–2025 (loan to Calviá 2020–21), MFK Tyumen from July 2025 (No. 39 there too), Spain U-19 2019 champion, Spain from 2022, Euro 2026;
 *    honours: UEFA Futsal Champions League 2022–23, 2023–24, 2024–25.
 *  - Wikipedia, "2024–25 UEFA Futsal Champions League" (raw; wiki-2024-25-uefa-futsal-cl.txt): final 4 May 2025, 20:00, Antarès, Le Mans:
 *    Palma Futsal 9–4 Kairat — Gordillo 6'03", Machado 18'00", Rivillos 18'56", Fabinho 22'12" 26'49" 27'28" 30'50", Neguinho 31'11",
 *    Mateus Maia 37'45"; Caio Ruiz 8'34", Tursagulov 32'32", Rashit 35'13", Arrieta 39'38". Semi-final 2 May: Sporting 0–3 Palma, Gordillo
 *    27'32" (his first of the two games).
 *  - UEFA.com, "Futsal Champions League final report: History-makers Palma retain title again" (4 May 2025;
 *    uefa-futsal-cl-2025-final-report.txt): "a rifled Jesús Gordillo opener – his second in two games"; Kairat level within three minutes;
 *    Palma the first team to win three straight titles; "the fans in green inside the arena".
 *  - UEFA match data, match 2044885 (match.uefa.com/v5/matches/2044885/lineups; uefa-api-2044885-lineups.json): Palma = home team, shirt
 *    colour #80ff00 (lime green); Kairat Almaty shirt colour #ff0000 (red); Palma starting five 3 Luan Muller (GK), 10 Rivillos, 17 Neguinho,
 *    28 Fabinho, 55 Marcelo; Gordillo No. 39 among the substitutes (so he came on before 6'03"); Kairat 2 Cavalcanti (GK), 6 Edson,
 *    12 Tursagulov, 17 Orazov (captain), 24 Arrieta.
 *  - Palma Futsal, "Tricampeones de Europa para ser eternos" (4 May 2025; palmafutsal-wp-2025-05.json): Palma kept the ball in Kairat's half
 *    ("La gran parte del partido se jugó en la pista rival. Posesión, circulación de balón"); Fabinho's two early shots just wide, then
 *    "el gol que marcó Gordillo. El pívot abrió de nuevo el marcador para júbilo de los casi trescientos aficionados que teñían de verde una
 *    de las esquinas del pabellón"; goals "1-0 Gordillo (min. 7)" (the 7th minute = 6'03"); Neguinho MVP; "primer club en la historia que
 *    gana tres UEFA Futsal Champions League consecutivas".
 * CONFIRMED: the competition, round, date, venue, city/country; the 9–4 score and the goal list (his goal 1–0 at 6'03", the first of the
 *  final); that it was a hard, "rifled" shot (not shown); team shirt colours (Palma lime green, Kairat red); his No. 39 and that he started on
 *  the bench; Palma's possession in Kairat's half; the corner of about 300 green-shirted Palma fans; three titles in a row.
 * INFERRED (never named in the narration): HOW and from where the goal was scored (not shown at all); which end Palma attacked; the moves
 *  of the Palma passing before the tilt (their general possession is confirmed, not these passes); where Gordillo ran to celebrate; which
 *  corner the fans were in (drawn far left); shorts/socks colours (Palma lime shirts, navy shorts, lime socks; Kairat red shirts, white
 *  shorts; Kairat's keeper in yellow); the hanging scoreboard's look; his build (1.80 m, short dark hair, light skin: playerAppearance.json;
 *  his beard is not drawn — the figure library has no beard). No video was reviewed. Chapters 2–3 are a coaching demonstration in
 *  training tops (no club, no match claimed); the finish is right-footed (the library default; his preferred foot is not confirmed).
 * Technique (chapters 2–3): the pivot holds his defender with his back and an arm (pinning him, so the defender must watch him and the ball
 *  at once); the moment the defender turns his head to the ball, the pivot spins off his blind side and arrives at the back post BEFORE the
 *  ball; he waits there ready — knees bent, body open to the passer and the goal — and strikes the ball the moment it arrives, with no
 *  control touch, so the keeper, who moved across with the winger, has no time to get back.
 * Players: the shared athlete library (./athlete.ts) through ONE adapter `athlete()` → drawAthlete (prev → hem/hair follow-through,
 *  motionSmear on strikes). Our stages are LEFT-handed (X right, Z away from the camera), so `projector()` maps library z → −Z.
 *  The strike is aimed: the shooter's root is solved from the contact point and the target (plantFor), so boot and ball always meet.
 * Timing: the SCRIPT's cues are estimated (≈2.7 words/s) until the lead voices it; `authored()` maps each chapter's recorded clock through
 *  the cue anchors back onto the authored choreography, so every action stays on its word after withTiming() moves the cues.
 * Inks: yellow (wood court, lights, diagram lines, cups), red (Kairat, posts, the crossed-out touch), green (Palma's lime shirts, the green
 *  corner, the back-post ring, ticks), navy (key line, stands, defenders' bibs). Composition: every scene is authored in a 1566×1080-unit
 *  box and cam() centres it on the FULL sheet (card window 1.45:1 → square). Phone heat: 4 plates; wide-shot figures 'low'; objects on
 *  twos, cameras on ones; all randomness seeded. */
import {withTiming,type NarrationTiming} from './timing';
import type {Sheet} from '../../paths/riso/sheet';
import {type RisoStory,type Scene,type Chapter,playChapters} from '../../paths/riso/story';
import {aperture} from '../../paths/riso/passage';
import {twos,sm,key,padKeys,linear,clamp,lerp,hash,blob,polyPath,ribbon,smoothPts,partial,rotPts,rectPath,easeOut,easeIO,easeOutBack,easeInOutSine,TAU,type Key,type Pt} from '../../paths/riso/motion';
import {sparkBurst,crescent} from '../../paths/riso/shapes';
import {drawAthlete,motionSmear,solve,strike,dribble,runCycle,runCadence,stand,backpedal,lunge,keeperSet,keeperDive,celebrate,posed,blendPose,STRIKE_CONTACT,
 type Pose,type AthleteStyle,type Projector,type Place,type V3,type InkFill,type Build} from './athlete';

const Y='yellow',R='red',G='green',K='navy';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- narration + timing
/** The narration (script.json mirrors it). Cue `words` are the match keys for the voice's word onsets; `at` and `seconds` are estimates. */
const SCRIPT:{label:string;text:string;tail:number;cues:string[];heads?:Record<string,string>}[]=[
 {label:'Live: the 2025 final',text:'Champions League final, 2025, in France. Palma, in green, play Kairat. Early on, the pivot Jesús Gordillo fires Palma in front! The green corner of fans goes wild. Palma win nine four, a third title in a row!',tail:2.4,
  cues:['Champions League','in green','play Kairat','Early on','fires Palma','green corner','Palma win','third title'],
  heads:{'Champions League':'Le Mans 2025 · final','play Kairat':'Palma v Kairat','fires Palma':'06:03 Gordillo · 1–0','green corner':'Palma fans','Palma win':'9–4','third title':'3 in a row'}},
 {label:'How he does it (demo)',text:'Watch how he does it. The winger drives down the side. Gordillo pins his defender, then slips to the back post. The pass comes across, and he hits it first time. Goal!',tail:2.2,
  cues:['Watch how','winger drives','Gordillo pins','slips to','back post','pass comes','first time','Goal'],
  heads:{'Watch how':'How he does it (demo)','Gordillo pins':'Pin the defender','back post':'Back post','first time':'First time!','Goal':'Goal!'}},
 {label:'Your turn',text:'Your turn. Be ready at the back post, and finish first time, with no extra touch!',tail:2.8,
  cues:['Your turn','Be ready','back post','finish first','no extra'],heads:{'Be ready':'Be ready at the back post','finish first':'Finish first time','no extra':'No extra touch'}},
];
/** Kokoro timing: null until the lead voices the film. After scripts/plays/kokoro-narrate.py writes
 * public/plays/narration/gordillo-futsal-signature/timing.json, add
 *   import timingJson from '../../../public/plays/narration/gordillo-futsal-signature/timing.json';
 * and set VOICE to `timingJson as NarrationTiming` (one line; every scene re-times itself from the cues). */
import timingJson from '../../../public/plays/narration/gordillo-futsal-signature/timing.json';
const VOICE:NarrationTiming|null=timingJson as NarrationTiming;
/** provisional word onsets: .26 s + .025 s a letter per word, pauses after , ; : . ! ? */
function estimate(text:string,cues:string[],tail:number){
 const words=[...text.matchAll(/\S+/g)],on:number[]=[];let t=.2;
 for(const m of words){on.push(t);const w=m[0];t+=.26+.025*w.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi,'').length;if(/[,;:]$/.test(w))t+=.22;if(/[.!?]$/.test(w))t+=.42;}
 let from=0;
 const cs=cues.map(c=>{const k=text.indexOf(c,from);if(k<0)throw new Error('gordillo: cue "'+c+'" not in the narration');from=k+c.length;const wi=words.findIndex(m=>(m.index??0)+m[0].length>k);return{at:+on[wi].toFixed(2),words:c};});
 return{seconds:+(t+tail).toFixed(2),cues:cs};
}
/** the authored clock: what the choreography was written against (the estimates, never re-timed) */
const AUTH=SCRIPT.map(c=>estimate(c.text,c.cues,c.tail));
const CHAPTERS:Chapter[]=withTiming(SCRIPT.map((c,i)=>{const e=AUTH[i];return{label:c.label,narration:c.text,seconds:e.seconds,
 cues:e.cues.map(q=>c.heads&&c.heads[q.words]!==undefined?{...q,headline:c.heads[q.words]}:q)};}),VOICE);
/** authored onset of the cue whose words start with w in chapter i (throws on a typo) */
const A=(i:number,w:string)=>{const c=AUTH[i].cues.find(q=>q.words.startsWith(w));if(!c)throw new Error('gordillo: no cue '+w);return c.at;};
const maps:number[][][]=[];
/** chapter time (recording) → authored scene time: piecewise linear through [0,0], each cue, the passage start and the end */
function authored(i:number,t:number){
 let m=maps[i];
 if(!m){const ch=CHAPTERS[i],Au=AUTH[i],raw:number[][]=[[0,0]];ch.cues.forEach((c,k)=>{if(Au.cues[k])raw.push([c.at,Au.cues[k].at]);});raw.push([ch.seconds-.65,Au.seconds-.65],[ch.seconds,Au.seconds]);
  m=[raw[0]];for(const p of raw.slice(1)){const q=m[m.length-1];if(p[0]>q[0]+.02&&p[1]>q[1]+.02&&p[0]<=ch.seconds&&(p[0]>=ch.seconds-.65||p[0]<ch.seconds-.65-.02))m.push(p);}maps[i]=m;}
 if(t<=0)return 0;for(let k=1;k<m.length;k++)if(t<=m[k][0])return m[k-1][1]+(m[k][1]-m[k-1][1])*(t-m[k-1][0])/(m[k][0]-m[k-1][0]);return m[m.length-1][1];
}
const clock=(i:number,t:number)=>({tt:authored(i,twos(t)),tc:authored(i,t)});
/** key() needs increasing times */
function mono(Kk:Key[],gap=.04):Key[]{const o:Key[]=[];for(const k of Kk){const t=o.length?Math.max(k[0] as number,(o[o.length-1][0] as number)+gap):k[0] as number;o.push([t,...k.slice(1)] as Key);}return o;}

// ---------------- camera: centre a 1566×1080 composition box on the canvas (card window or full screen) ----------------
const BOX_W=1566,BOX_H=1080;
function cam(s:Sheet,x:number,y:number,zoom:number,rot=0){
 const base=Math.min(s.W/BOX_W,s.H/BOX_H),S=zoom*base*s.arrival,c=Math.cos(rot),sn=Math.sin(rot),dx=(s.W/2-s.cx)/S,dy=(s.H/2-s.cy)/S;
 s.camera(x-(c*dx+sn*dy),y-(-sn*dx+c*dy),zoom*base/Math.max(.01,s.fit),rot);
}
const kv=(T:number,K0:Key[])=>key(T,padKeys(mono(K0),[0]),easeInOutSine,true)[0]||0;

// ---------------- stage: a perspective camera over the court floor (metres → world units); X right, Y up, Z away ----------------
type Stage={F:number;eye:number;cx:number;cz:number};
const proj=(st:Stage,X:number,Yh:number,Z:number):Pt=>{const k=st.F/Math.max(.25,Z-st.cz);return[(X-st.cx)*k,(st.eye-Yh)*k];};
const kAt=(st:Stage,Z:number)=>st.F/Math.max(.25,Z-st.cz);
const BALL_R=.11;
const pulse=(t:number,t0:number,len=1)=>t<t0?0:Math.min(1,(t-t0)*10)*Math.exp(-(t-t0)*2.4/len);
const lin3=(a:V3,b:V3,u:number):V3=>[lerp(a[0],b[0],u),lerp(a[1],b[1],u),lerp(a[2],b[2],u)];
const quad3=(a:V3,m:V3,b:V3,u:number):V3=>{const p=(1-u)*(1-u),q=2*u*(1-u),r=u*u;return[p*a[0]+q*m[0]+r*b[0],p*a[1]+q*m[1]+r*b[1],p*a[2]+q*m[2]+r*b[2]];};

// ---------------- geometry helpers ----------------
function dashGaps(pts:Pt[],dash:number):[number,number][]{let L=0;for(let i=1;i<pts.length;i++)L+=Math.hypot(pts[i][0]-pts[i-1][0],pts[i][1]-pts[i-1][1]);const n=Math.max(1,Math.floor(L/dash)),g:[number,number][]=[];for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const u=(i+.55)/n;g.push([u,u+.45/n]);}return g;}
/** a dashed hand-drawn line, knocked out to paper first so the ink prints clean over the court */
function dashed(s:Sheet,ink:string,pts:Pt[],width:number,seed:number,o:{dash?:number;cov?:number;progress?:number;ko?:boolean}={}){const{dash=width*4.5,cov=1,progress=1,ko=true}=o;const line=progress>=1?smoothPts(pts,false,8):partial(smoothPts(pts,false,8),progress);if(line.length<2)return;const p=ribbon(line,width,{seed,pressure:.3,taper:.2,wobble:1.2,gaps:dashGaps(line,dash)});if(ko)s.knockout(p);s.fill(ink,p,cov);}
function arrowHead(s:Sheet,ink:string,pts:Pt[],size:number,cov=1){if(pts.length<2)return;const a=pts[pts.length-1],b=pts[Math.max(0,pts.length-3)],ang=Math.atan2(a[1]-b[1],a[0]-b[0]);const q=rotPts([[size*.35,0],[-size*.75,-size*.62],[-size*.45,0],[-size*.75,size*.62]],ang).map(p=>[p[0]+a[0],p[1]+a[1]] as Pt),path=polyPath(q,true);s.knockout(path);s.fill(ink,path,cov);}
function floorRing(st:Stage,X:number,Z:number,r:number,n=24):Pt[]{const out:Pt[]=[];for(let i=0;i<n;i++){const a=i/n*TAU;out.push(proj(st,X+Math.cos(a)*r,0,Z+Math.sin(a)*r));}return out;}
function floorStrip(st:Stage,pts:Pt[],hw:number):Pt[]{const L:Pt[]=[],Rr:Pt[]=[];for(let i=0;i<pts.length;i++){const a=pts[Math.max(0,i-1)],b=pts[Math.min(pts.length-1,i+1)],dx=b[0]-a[0],dz=b[1]-a[1],l=Math.hypot(dx,dz)||1,nx=-dz/l*hw,nz=dx/l*hw;L.push(proj(st,pts[i][0]+nx,0,pts[i][1]+nz));Rr.push(proj(st,pts[i][0]-nx,0,pts[i][1]-nz));}return[...L,...Rr.reverse()];}
function floorQuad(st:Stage,x0:number,z0:number,x1:number,z1:number):Pt[]{const za=Math.max(z0,st.cz+.4),zb=Math.max(z1,st.cz+.45);return[proj(st,x0,0,za),proj(st,x1,0,za),proj(st,x1,0,zb),proj(st,x0,0,zb)];}
function floorDashRing(s:Sheet,st:Stage,ink:string,X:number,Z:number,r:number,w:number,seed:number,g=1){if(g<=.02)return;const q=floorRing(st,X,Z,r*g,26),p=ribbon([...q,q[0]],w,{seed,close:true,wobble:1,gaps:dashGaps(q,w*3.4)});s.knockout(p);s.fill(ink,p,1);}
/** a floor path (metres) drawn as a dashed line on the court */
const floorPts=(st:Stage,pts:[number,number][])=>pts.map(p=>proj(st,p[0],0,p[1]));
/** a big tick: green stroke, navy misregistered echo */
function tickMark(s:Sheet,c:Pt,S:number,seed:number){const tk:Pt[]=[[-.5,0],[-.15,.38],[.55,-.5]].map(q=>[c[0]+q[0]*S,c[1]+q[1]*S] as Pt);
 s.knockout(ribbon(tk,S*.34,{seed:seed+1,taper:.1,wobble:1}));s.fill(K,ribbon(tk.map(q=>[q[0]+7,q[1]+7] as Pt),S*.24,{seed,taper:.2,wobble:1}),.5);s.fill(G,ribbon(tk,S*.24,{seed:seed+2,taper:.2,wobble:1}));}
/** a trophy cup: yellow bowl, stem and base with two handles, a navy key line */
function cup(s:Sheet,x:number,y:number,S:number,seed:number){
 // the bowl: left rim → round the bottom → right rim; then the stem and the foot
 const bowl:Pt[]=[];for(let k=0;k<=12;k++){const a=k/12*Math.PI;bowl.push([x-Math.cos(a)*S*.5,y-S*.55+Math.sin(a)*S*.62]);}
 const foot:Pt[]=[[x+S*.07,y+S*.05],[x+S*.07,y+S*.3],[x+S*.3,y+S*.42],[x-S*.3,y+S*.42],[x-S*.07,y+S*.3],[x-S*.07,y+S*.05]];
 const body=new Path2D();body.addPath(polyPath(bowl,true));body.addPath(polyPath(foot,true));
 const handles=new Path2D();handles.addPath(ribbon([[x-S*.46,y-S*.45],[x-S*.76,y-S*.4],[x-S*.62,y-S*.08],[x-S*.32,y-S*.02]],S*.09,{seed,taper:.1,wobble:.6}));
 handles.addPath(ribbon([[x+S*.46,y-S*.45],[x+S*.76,y-S*.4],[x+S*.62,y-S*.08],[x+S*.32,y-S*.02]],S*.09,{seed:seed+1,taper:.1,wobble:.6}));
 s.knockout(body);s.knockout(handles);s.fill(Y,body);s.fill(Y,handles);
 const key0=new Path2D();key0.addPath(ribbon([...bowl,bowl[0]],Math.max(3,S*.05),{seed:seed+2,close:true,wobble:.6}));key0.addPath(ribbon([...foot,foot[0]],Math.max(3,S*.05),{seed:seed+3,close:true,wobble:.6}));
 s.fill(K,key0,.85);
}

// ---------------- players: the shared athlete library ----------------
/** Our stages are LEFT-handed (X right, Z away, Y up); the library is right-handed: library z = −Z. */
function projector(st:Stage):Projector{return{eye:[st.cx,st.eye,-st.cz] as V3,project(p:V3){const Z=-p[2],q=proj(st,p[0],p[1],Z);return[q[0],q[1],Z-st.cz];},scale(p:V3){return kAt(st,-p[2]);}};}
const placeAt=(X:number,Z:number,yaw:number):Place=>({x:X,z:-Z,yaw});
const toMine=(p:V3):V3=>[p[0],p[1],-p[2]];
/** yaw that faces the floor direction (dX,dZ) in our stage (library yaw 0 faces +X; + turns toward +Z here) */
const yawTo=(dX:number,dZ:number)=>Math.atan2(dZ,dX);
const FACE_LEFT=Math.PI,FACE_CAMERA=-Math.PI/2,FACE_AWAY=Math.PI/2;
const SKIN_L:InkFill[]=[[Y,.86],[R,.26]],SKIN_M:InkFill[]=[[Y,.72],[R,.4]],SKIN_D:InkFill[]=[[R,.6],[K,.34]];
/** Gordillo: 1.80 m (inferred), short dark hair, light skin (playerAppearance.json); Palma No. 39 (UEFA line-up) in lime green (feed #80ff00) */
const BUILD_G:Build={height:1.8,bulk:1.05};
const GORD:AthleteStyle={shirt:G,shorts:K,socks:G,boots:K,skin:SKIN_L,hair:K,line:K,trim:'paper',number:39,numberInk:'paper',hairStyle:'short',build:BUILD_G,seed:39};
/** the demonstration: Gordillo in a yellow training top (no club, no match claimed) */
const GORD_DEMO:AthleteStyle={...GORD,shirt:[Y,.95],trim:K,number:null,socks:K,seed:40};
/** Palma outfield: lime shirts (UEFA feed), navy shorts, lime socks (inferred) */
const PAL=(n:number):AthleteStyle=>({shirt:G,shorts:K,socks:G,boots:K,skin:n%3===1?SKIN_M:n%3===2?SKIN_D:SKIN_L,hair:K,line:K,trim:'paper',hairStyle:(['short','bald','curly','short'] as const)[n%4],build:{height:1.7+hash(n,3)*.12},seed:30+n});
/** Kairat: red shirts (UEFA feed #ff0000), white shorts, red socks (inferred) */
const KAI=(n:number):AthleteStyle=>({shirt:R,shorts:'paper',socks:R,boots:K,skin:n%3===0?SKIN_D:n%3===1?SKIN_M:SKIN_L,hair:K,line:K,trim:'paper',hairStyle:(['short','curly','bald','short'] as const)[n%4],build:{height:1.72+hash(n,4)*.12},seed:50+n});
/** Kairat's goalkeeper: yellow long sleeves (inferred colour) */
